  "caption": "Quinn tried putting socks on standing up and wobbled like a circus act, then nearly tripped on a kerb. The plan: just walk more.\n\nKay explained that balance is trainable at any age, and combining balance and strength work has good evidence for lowering falls risk. Walking alone isn't quite enough.\n\nWhat can help: progressing from a narrow stance near a sturdy chair, to no hands, to head turns, to doing two things at once, plus building leg strength. In studies, regular sessions adding up to about three hours a week helped most.\n\nGet assessed first if you've had recent falls or feel unsteady, and get checked for a possible fracture, sudden weakness, chest pain or new nerve symptoms.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
